# TODO - Empirical Malbolge synthesis scaling law

## Objective

Measure how verified synthesis cost changes with challenge difficulty,
self-modification footprint, layout coupling, target-state entropy, and reusable
catalogue coverage. Compare multiple search/composition strategies under equal
budgets and fit empirical models instead of assuming a complexity class.

## Acceptance

- Challenge families vary declared difficulty dimensions while preserving stable
  semantic oracles and reproducible identities.
- Blind/enumerative, structured deterministic, reusable-catalogue, stochastic or
  learned, and available accelerator-backed strategies are compared under
  equivalent budgets where applicable.
- Cold search, warm reuse, verification, linking, cache, and invalidation costs
  are reported separately.
- Results include capacity curves, marginal-cost measurements, uncertainty, and
  failed model fits; no preferred O-notation is chosen before evidence exists.
- The verifier remains the correctness authority regardless of search strategy.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `docs/research/studies/`,
  `benchmarks/research/`, `benchmarks/challenges/`, `algorithms/`.
- Required evidence: raw samples, model-fit artifacts, capacity curves,
  catalogue/version provenance, verifier identity, and threats to validity.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `superoptimization-research-program`,
  `benchmark-and-statistical-evidence-protocol`,
  `parametric-compiler-challenge-generator`, `reusable-block-catalogue`,
  `stochastic-and-guided-search`.
